<title>ITALY: Merloni names Caio as Managing Director.</title>
<headline>Merloni names Caio as Managing Director.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian household appliance maker Merloni Elettrodomestici said it had appointed ex-Olivetti chief executive Francesco Caio as its new managing director.</p>
<p>Merloni, which owns brands such as Ariston, Indesit and Schlotes, said in a statement that Caio would have full responsibility for operating and financial matters at the company.</p>
<p>Caio had been chief executive of struggling information technology group Olivetti for only two months when he left the company in early September. Before that he was head of mobile phone group Omnitel where Olivetti has around a 35 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
